      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2511.21699v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        We present Cacheback Decoding, a training-free and model-agnostic speculative decoding method that exploits the locality in language to accelerate Large <span class="search-hit mathjax">Language</span> <span class="search-hit mathjax">Model</span> (LLM) <span class="search-hit mathjax">inference</span>. Cacheback leverages only Least Recently Used (LRU) cache tables of token n-grams to generate dr&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2511.21699v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2511.21699v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
