      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2511.21699v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        We present Cacheback Decoding, a training-free and model-agnostic speculative decoding method that exploits the locality in language to accelerate Large <span class="search-hit mathjax">Language</span> <span class="search-hit mathjax">Model</span> (LLM) <span class="search-hit mathjax">inference</span>. Cacheback leverages only Least Recently Used (LRU) cache tables of token n-grams to generate draft sequences. Cacheback achieves state-of-the-art performance among comparable methods despite its minimalist design, and its simplicity allows easy integration into existing systems. Cacheback also shows potential for fast adaptation to new domains.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2511.21699v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2511.21699v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
